      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Family Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1"><h2>Family patterns across generations</h2><p>Parents want to be there for their children and do many things better than they themselves experienced, and yet unhelpful behavior shows up again under stress. Children, in turn, want to protect their parents: with fine antennae they unconsciously take on parents' assignments, responsibility or emotions, or get into conflict with them. The multigenerational perspective takes into account that family themes and patterns are passed on from grandparents via parents to children, and that this is often where starting points for change lie.</p></div>
          <div class="rd-clamp rd-col rd-text c2"><h2>Flexible design of settings according to themes and assignment</h2><p>A strength of systemic family therapy and counseling is that the family members involved can talk with each other in changing constellations.</p>
            <div class="rd-kernsatz"><p>We go by what helps you.</p></div>
            <p>You decide who takes part in the sessions: parents and children together, only the parents, the siblings, or even the grandparents. If needed, individual sessions with children or parents are possible, and further people can join.</p>
            <button class="rd-readmore" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="faq-toggle"></span><span class="rd-readmore-t">Read more</span></button>
            <p class="rd-keep"><a class="rd-more-link" href="{{ '/en/systemische-therapie/' | url }}#arbeitsverstaendnis">More on my systemic professional understanding<span class="rd-chev"></span></a></p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="snap-section rd-sec rd-tint rd-ez rd-ez-lists rd-mtabs" id="anlaesse" data-index="2">
      <div class="about-band offers-band"></div>
      <div class="rd-inner">
        <div class="rd-eyebrow">Family Therapy &amp; Counseling</div>
        <div class="rd-mtabbar" role="tablist"><button class="is-active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mtab="0">Occasions</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mtab="1">How it helps</button></div>
        <div class="rd-cols">
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c1 rd-mpanel is-active" data-mpanel="0"><h2>What can be occasions for family therapy?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>Parents worry about their child's behavior</li>
              <li>Open or underlying conflicts burden family life</li>
              <li>Difficult life transitions, for example the move from daycare to school, a change of job or residence, a child moving out</li>
              <li>Struggling with expectations, loyalties, values as well as closeness and distance makes living together harder</li>
              <li>Illness, loss or grief burden the family</li>
              <li>Parents doubt their relationship, are facing a separation or are already separated</li>
            </ul></div>
          <div class="rd-col rd-text c2 rd-mpanel" data-mpanel="1"><h2>What can family therapy help with?</h2>
            <ul class="rd-bullets">
              <li>Understanding the behavior of individual family members as a pointer to themes of the whole family</li>
              <li>Making roles, assignments and expectations between generations visible</li>
              <li>Recognizing relationship and communication patterns that run unconsciously and changing them in a desired direction</li>
              <li>Getting into conversation with each other, including about difficult topics</li>
              <li>Approaching emotional and vulnerable topics in a safe setting</li>
              <li>Trying out new ways of dealing with conflict, closeness and distance</li>
              <li>Shaping life transitions and changes together</li>
            </ul></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

